          "number": 10,
          "letter": "J",
          "english": "Using voice interaction feels far more intimate than surfing the net the old-fashioned way. This is intentional as the informal tone of the assistant helps create an emotional attachment. But if something speaks, it must also listen. Our phones are always near us and they are collecting data about us all the time. This has already raised privacy concerns. The American Civil Liberties Union has stated that digital assistants create a threat to privacy from hackers. Some people have other concerns. They worry assistants will one day be used to deliver advertising directly to us.",
          "chinese": "使用语音交互比以老式方式上网感觉更加亲密。这是有意为之,因为助手的非正式语气有助于建立情感依附。但如果某物会说话,它也必须会倾听。我们的手机总是在我们身边,它们一直在收集关于我们的数据。这已经引发了隐私担忧。美国公民自由联盟表示,数字助手对黑客造成的隐私威胁。有些人还有其他担忧。他们担心助手有一天会被用来直接向我们投放广告。",
