          "number": 11,
          "letter": "K",
          "english": "But digital voices need more personality to make them popular. Robots are not yet witty, Siri is boring. The benefits of using voice instead of tapping fingers obviously depend on the context. Doctors completing online forms about their patients by speech, for example, can dictate 150 words a minute, three times faster than typing on a keyboard. This enables them to spend less time on administration and more time with patients.",
          "chinese": "但数字语音需要更多个性才能使它们受欢迎。机器人还不够风趣,Siri很无聊。使用语音而不是敲击手指的好处显然取决于具体情境。例如,医生通过语音完成关于患者的在线表格,可以每分钟口述150个单词,比在键盘上打字快三倍。这使他们能够在行政事务上花更少时间,在患者身上花更多时间。",
