          "number": 13,
          "letter": "M",
          "english": "Using voice also makes sense when you're doing other things with your hands. Think about when you're cooking, and you just want to know what the next step in the recipe is. Your hands are covered with oil; you're not going to get on the iPad, so it's a lot more natural to talk. And speech obviously makes sense when you're driving. In the U.S., 29% of drivers admit they surf behind the wheel, according to insurance firm State Farm. This is up from 13% in 2009. No wonder using mobile phones while driving causes more crashes a year than drink driving, says the U.S. National Safety Council.",
          "chinese": "当你的手正在做其他事情时,使用语音也很有意义。想想当你在做饭时,你只想知道食谱的下一步是什么。你的手上沾满了油,你不会去拿iPad,所以说话要自然得多。而且在开车时语音显然很有意义。根据保险公司State Farm的数据,在美国,29%的司机承认他们在开车时上网。这一比例从2009年的13%上升。美国国家安全委员会表示,难怪开车时使用手机造成的交通事故比酒驾还多。",
